  "rationale": [
    "The imported callback has the real C ABI [*c]c_int. Direct forwarding invokes the pinned Zig C-pointer coercion to the helper's unchanged nonoptional *c_int.",
    "Taking the address of flags[0] yields *allowzero c_int and loses that C-pointer coercion rule.",
    "The production hook is reached only when flags_only is true, defined as desc == NULL && pflags != NULL. No nullable path is fabricated or accepted.",
    "The correction preserves query ordering, flags writes, all 28 control declarations and assertions. No weaker pointer type, manual integer conversion, extra fallback or bypass is introduced."
  ],
  "authority_files": [
    {
      "path": "C:\\Users\\adyba\\pi-zig\\main\\vendor\\quickjs\\quickjs.h",
      "bytes": 113474,
      "sha256": "5D18897CF447EDF7C4CD1453EBA1E23F5CBCBAFC5478C6270CEA573739202D6C",
      "source_ranges": [
        {
          "first": 836,
          "last": 841,
          "text": "    /* Optional attribute-only lookup. Called only when the VM requests\n       existence/flags without a descriptor value. obj and prop are borrowed.\n       Return -1 on exception, 0 if absent, or 1 after writing *flags.\n       A missing hook retains the get_own_property temporary-descriptor path. */\n    int (*get_own_property_flags)(JSContext *ctx, int *flags,\n                                  JSValueConst obj, JSAtom prop);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "C:\\Users\\adyba\\pi-zig\\main\\vendor\\quickjs\\quickjs.c",
      "bytes": 2399340,
      "sha256": "2D625940688B1BE334585048731B42F4F1E3CDCCA60CE6B5F6D0478D7274AFC2",
      "source_ranges": [
        {
          "first": 11469,
          "last": 11487,
          "text": "\n/* Return -1 if exception,\n   false if the property does not exist, true if it exists. If true is\n   returned, the property descriptor 'desc' is filled present. */\nstatic int JS_GetOwnPropertyInternal2(JSContext *ctx, JSPropertyDescriptor *desc,\n                                      JSObject *p, JSAtom prop, int *pflags)\n{\n    JSShapeProperty *prs;\n    JSProperty *pr;\n    int flags_only = (desc == NULL && pflags != NULL);\n\nretry:\n    prs = find_own_property(&pr, p, prop);\n    if (prs) {\n        if (desc) {\n            desc->flags = prs->flags & JS_PROP_C_W_E;\n            desc->getter = JS_UNDEFINED;\n            desc->setter = JS_UNDEFINED;\n            desc->value = JS_UNDEFINED;"
        },
        {
          "first": 11549,
          "last": 11554,
          "text": "        } else {\n            const JSClassExoticMethods *em = ctx->rt->class_array[p->class_id].exotic;\n            if (flags_only && em && em->get_own_property_flags) {\n                return em->get_own_property_flags(ctx, pflags,\n                                                  JS_MKPTR(JS_TAG_OBJECT, p),\n                                                  prop);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "C:\\Users\\adyba\\pi-zig\\toolchain\\zig-x86_64-windows-0.16.0\\doc\\langref.html",
      "bytes": 983945,
      "sha256": "095DAA2D9F1262FB8BC00AFBB44D386F20363FD930E400BF703A8BC4255A4FFD",
      "source_ranges": [
        {
          "first": 14471,
          "last": 14496,
          "text": "      <h3 id=\"C-Pointers\"><a href=\"#toc-C-Pointers\">C Pointers</a> <a class=\"hdr\" href=\"#C-Pointers\">\u00a7</a></h3>\n\n      <p>\n      This type is to be avoided whenever possible. The only valid reason for using a C pointer is in\n      auto-generated code from translating C code.\n      </p>\n      <p>\n      When importing C header files, it is ambiguous whether pointers should be translated as\n      single-item pointers (<code>*T</code>) or many-item pointers (<code>[*]T</code>).\n      C pointers are a compromise so that Zig code can utilize translated header files directly.\n      </p>\n      <p><code>[*c]T</code> - C pointer.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Supports all the syntax of the other two pointer types (<code>*T</code>) and (<code>[*]T</code>).</li>\n        <li>Coerces to other pointer types, as well as <a href=\"#Optional-Pointers\">Optional Pointers</a>.\n            When a C pointer is coerced to a non-optional pointer, safety-checked\n            <a href=\"#Illegal-Behavior\">Illegal Behavior</a> occurs if the address is 0.\n        </li>\n        <li>Allows address 0. On non-freestanding targets, dereferencing address 0 is safety-checked\n            <a href=\"#Illegal-Behavior\">Illegal Behavior</a>. Optional C pointers introduce another bit to keep track of\n            null, just like <code>?<span class=\"tok-type\">usize</span></code>. Note that creating an optional C pointer\n            is unnecessary as one can use normal <a href=\"#Optional-Pointers\">Optional Pointers</a>.\n        </li>\n        <li>Supports <a href=\"#Type-Coercion\">Type Coercion</a> to and from integers.</li>\n        <li>Supports comparison with integers.</li>\n        <li>Does not support Zig-only pointer attributes such as alignment. Use normal <a href=\"#Pointers\">Pointers</a>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
